From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:13:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Shape brand new chunks on a worker thread

New chunks now go through ChunkGenExecutor, built on the same AsynchronousExecutor
that has been deferring chunk loads for years: stage 1 shapes the chunk on a
worker, stage 2 finishes it on the server thread. The route in is the callback
form of ChunkProviderServer.getChunkAt, which callers have always allowed to
answer later, so none of them notice.

A caller that needs the chunk immediately still goes through the queue, which
joins a worker that has already started that chunk instead of shaping it twice.
Population of a neighbour asks for exactly those chunks, so this is the common
case, not a corner.

Each shaping thread gets its own copy of the generator; three are built up front
on the server thread so a worker never has to touch the world to make one. The
carvers get the copy's own WorldChunkManager, because World.getBiome would
otherwise read the chunk map and the shared BiomeCache from a worker - it
answers the same thing, since the chunk being carved is never loaded yet.

Worlds with a plugin chunk generator, and anything but a plain WorldChunkManager,
keep generating on the server thread. pandaspigot.yml async-chunk-shaping turns
it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

